      <h2>5. How AI Can Be Used in Modern Random Chat</h2>

      <p>Artificial intelligence can support online communication platforms in several ways, particularly around moderation, spam detection and automated analysis. However, AI systems are not perfect and their capabilities vary significantly between platforms.</p>

      <h3>5.1 Automated Content Moderation</h3>

      <p>Machine-learning systems can be used to identify potentially inappropriate content or behavior. Depending on the platform, automated systems may flag content for review or trigger predefined safety actions.</p>

      <p>Users should not assume that an automated moderation system will detect every violation. Reporting tools and clear community guidelines remain important.</p>

      <h3>5.2 Matching and Recommendations</h3>

      <p>Some platforms use algorithms to determine which users should be connected. Possible factors can include language, interests, location or other preferences, depending on the service.</p>

      <p>Users should check the platform's documentation rather than assuming that an algorithm is actually matching people based on compatibility.</p>

      <h3>5.3 The Limits of AI Moderation</h3>

      <p>AI can make mistakes. Context, sarcasm, cultural differences and ambiguous behavior can be difficult for automated systems to interpret.</p>

